WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.190
A student of mine used up her

2
00:00:02.190 --> 00:00:03.650
whole data bundle in a week.

3
00:00:04.350 --> 00:00:06.390
Not on videos: on chatting

4
00:00:06.390 --> 00:00:07.690
with an AI agent!

5
00:00:08.410 --> 00:00:10.150
Every question went to a

6
00:00:10.150 --> 00:00:12.230
big computer far away.

7
00:00:12.880 --> 00:00:14.000
Is there another way?

8
00:00:15.210 --> 00:00:17.770
Today: what an agent costs in data,

9
00:00:18.170 --> 00:00:20.930
money and privacy, and how to choose.

10
00:00:22.250 --> 00:00:25.170
Big agents run in the cloud: huge

11
00:00:25.170 --> 00:00:27.310
models on computers far away.

12
00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:29.920
Your question travels there and

13
00:00:29.920 --> 00:00:31.120
back over the network.

14
00:00:31.860 --> 00:00:35.000
Darsi Tiny is different: it runs on

15
00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:37.040
your phone, so nothing leaves it.

16
00:00:38.210 --> 00:00:39.950
Take one weather request.

17
00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:44.240
Darsi Tiny reads about sixty tokens and

18
00:00:44.240 --> 00:00:47.020
answers in about a second, with no data.

19
00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:49.920
A cloud model reads about two and

20
00:00:49.920 --> 00:00:52.280
a half thousand, since the tools

21
00:00:52.280 --> 00:00:53.600
are described every time.

22
00:00:54.260 --> 00:00:56.100
That’s about eighteen kilobytes,

23
00:00:56.420 --> 00:00:58.380
and five seconds on 2G.

24
00:00:59.550 --> 00:01:02.330
At twenty requests a day, a month of cloud

25
00:01:02.330 --> 00:01:04.590
requests is about eleven megabytes.

26
00:01:05.270 --> 00:01:07.690
Darsi Tiny’s one download is

27
00:01:07.690 --> 00:01:09.250
two point eight megabytes.

28
00:01:09.980 --> 00:01:11.480
After about a hundred and fifty

29
00:01:11.480 --> 00:01:13.780
requests, the cloud has used more.

30
00:01:15.030 --> 00:01:16.390
You can work this out in Python.

31
00:01:17.210 --> 00:01:20.650
Multiply the kilobytes for one request by

32
00:01:20.650 --> 00:01:22.670
the requests a day and the days.

33
00:01:23.310 --> 00:01:25.150
Then divide by a thousand for

34
00:01:25.150 --> 00:01:26.870
megabytes: ten point eight.

35
00:01:28.050 --> 00:01:28.530
Quick check!

36
00:01:29.140 --> 00:01:32.100
You’re on a bus with no signal, and you

37
00:01:32.100 --> 00:01:33.700
want to ask an agent something.

38
00:01:34.440 --> 00:01:36.260
Which one can still answer?

39
00:01:37.530 --> 00:01:39.090
The small model on your phone:

40
00:01:39.450 --> 00:01:40.570
it doesn’t need a signal.

41
00:01:41.270 --> 00:01:43.450
But remember what it can’t do.

42
00:01:44.050 --> 00:01:46.730
Darsi Tiny knows ten school tools

43
00:01:46.730 --> 00:01:48.630
and almost nothing else.

44
00:01:49.310 --> 00:01:51.450
A big cloud model knows far

45
00:01:51.450 --> 00:01:53.390
more, and that’s the trade.

46
00:01:54.580 --> 00:01:56.140
Cost isn’t only money.

47
00:01:56.870 --> 00:01:59.470
Whatever you type into a cloud agent

48
00:01:59.470 --> 00:02:01.650
leaves your phone and is stored on

49
00:02:01.650 --> 00:02:02.950
someone else’s computers.

50
00:02:03.890 --> 00:02:06.710
It may be kept, read by staff, or

51
00:02:06.710 --> 00:02:08.430
used to train the next model.

52
00:02:09.670 --> 00:02:12.710
So never type these into a cloud agent.

53
00:02:13.490 --> 00:02:15.190
Your passwords and codes.

54
00:02:16.010 --> 00:02:19.050
Your address, phone number or ID number.

55
00:02:19.690 --> 00:02:22.430
And other people’s private things: a

56
00:02:22.430 --> 00:02:25.010
friend’s photo, their marks, their

57
00:02:25.010 --> 00:02:25.370
secrets.

58
00:02:26.840 --> 00:02:28.920
In the app, run the weather request

59
00:02:28.920 --> 00:02:31.580
and note the tokens and the time.

60
00:02:32.280 --> 00:02:35.040
Switch to 2G and compare the cloud.

61
00:02:35.680 --> 00:02:37.500
Then set your data price and

62
00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:39.620
requests a day, and see a month.

63
00:02:40.840 --> 00:02:41.340
Your turn.

64
00:02:41.950 --> 00:02:43.750
You want help with your diary, which

65
00:02:43.750 --> 00:02:45.590
is full of private thoughts.

66
00:02:46.070 --> 00:02:47.810
Where is it safest to ask?

67
00:02:49.000 --> 00:02:51.060
On your phone, or not at all.

68
00:02:51.720 --> 00:02:53.860
Remember: cloud agents cost

69
00:02:53.860 --> 00:02:56.840
data, money and a signal, and

70
00:02:56.840 --> 00:02:58.360
your words leave the phone.

71
00:02:58.950 --> 00:03:00.970
Phone models are cheap and

72
00:03:00.970 --> 00:03:02.770
private, but know little.

73
00:03:03.430 --> 00:03:06.310
Never type passwords or others’ secrets.

74
00:03:07.690 --> 00:03:10.610
Try it yourself: check how much data your

75
00:03:10.610 --> 00:03:13.550
phone used last month, and on which apps.

76
00:03:14.200 --> 00:03:16.600
Guess how much went on one AI app.

77
00:03:17.210 --> 00:03:18.950
Then decide one thing you

78
00:03:18.950 --> 00:03:20.470
will never type into it.
